  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Boundaries that hold",
      "items": [
        "Every /garden/secrets/ page, the /garden/ landing page and every approval need an Access JWT the vault verifies; only Cloudflare adds it",
        "The tunnel forwards only /garden/secrets and /garden/ to the vault; /mcp and /redeem answer to Host secret-broker with no Origin",
        "lettucectl check refuses a vault without read_only or cap_drop ALL, with a host mount, or whose volume another service mounts",
        "The data key lives only in the vault process while unlocked; a lock drops handles and uncollected values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Not a boundary",
      "items": [
        "BFF and app-server share one network namespace; agents run as root in app-server",
        "Agents can call /mcp and /redeem themselves, so approval is the gate",
        "vault-run keeps values out of the conversation, but an agent could redeem a handle directly"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown",
      "items": [
        "Opt-in sidecars: searxng, ddg-mcp, google-mcp, gmail-triggers, pipelock, channel-gateway (it also joins the app-server namespace)",
        "The LLM provider that app-server calls",
        "lettucectl on the host: builds and checks each stack, installs vault-run with lettucectl skills"
      ]
    }
  ]
